From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:08:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(miniwin): drain the thread's proxied calls in
 PeekMessageA on the web

With -sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD a game whose message loop blocks never returns its
worker to the browser. SDL's DOM event handlers are proxied to the worker
and run only when it drains its queue, which a busy loop does only while
it sleeps, so a key press and its release can reach SDL together and a
game that polls SDL's keyboard state never sees the key down. PeekMessageA
now drains the calling thread's queue first when it is not the main
browser thread.

diff --git a/miniwin/src/windows/windowmessages.cpp b/miniwin/src/windows/windowmessages.cpp
index a03c088..9747c84 100644
--- a/miniwin/src/windows/windowmessages.cpp
+++ b/miniwin/src/windows/windowmessages.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 #include "miniwin/windows.h"
 
 #include <SDL3/SDL.h>
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#include <emscripten/threading.h>
+#endif
 #include <deque>
 #include <string>
 #include <unordered_map>
@@ -419,6 +422,16 @@ LRESULT DefWindowProcA(HWND hWnd, UINT Msg, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam)
 
 BOOL PeekMessageA(LPMSG lpMsg, HWND hWnd, UINT wMsgFilterMin, UINT wMsgFilterMax, UINT wRemoveMsg)
 {
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && defined(__EMSCRIPTEN_PTHREADS__)
+	// A game that blocks on a worker (-sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD) never returns to
+	// the browser, so the DOM events SDL's handlers proxy to its thread run
+	// only when that thread drains its queue. Drain it here, once per pump,
+	// so a key press and its release reach SDL's keyboard state in
+	// different frames rather than together.
+	if (!emscripten_is_main_browser_thread()) {
+		emscripten_current_thread_process_queued_calls();
+	}
+#endif
 	SDL_Event event;
 	while (SDL_PollEvent(&event)) {
 		Translate(event);
